From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:03:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/49] S020 (check): pack types are collected while the index
 files are loaded

From the S020 incumbent (T2). Checker.LoadIndex needs, for every pack,
whether its blobs are of one type (the mixed-pack hint) and iterates
over those packs for the duplicate-pack hints. It walked the whole
loaded index again for that. When the load starts from an empty index
every stored blob passes through the load callback, where the blobs are
already grouped by pack: the type summary is taken there, one map
update per pack group. A load that starts from a non-empty index keeps
the walk after the load.

This is not lock-wait work: it changes how LoadIndex computes a value
it used to compute by a second walk, wherever LoadIndex runs.

New: internal/repository/checker_pack_types.go and its test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
